3. COMPLETE WEAPON SELECTOR REDESIGN

This is one of the most important improvements.

The current weapon selection buttons occupy too much space and may become cluttered when additional weapons are introduced.

I want the weapon selector to become more minimalistic, compact, flexible, and expandable.

Do not keep adding individual weapon buttons horizontally or vertically until they occupy the entire bottom area of the screen.

Design a dynamic weapon selection interface that can accommodate future weapons without becoming cluttered.

3.1 NEW WEAPON SELECTOR DESIGN

Replace the current crowded weapon button arrangement with a modern compact weapon selector.

Recommended design:

- One compact primary weapon selector.
- A clear selected weapon icon.
- Weapon name or short label.
- Small weapon number or selection indicator where useful.
- Subtle futuristic border.
- Dark translucent background.
- Clean visual hierarchy.

When the player taps the selector, open a compact weapon selection panel.

The panel displays the available weapons in an organized grid or scrollable list.

Each weapon entry should contain:

- Weapon icon.
- Weapon name.
- Short description where appropriate.
- Weapon type.
- Unlock status.
- Selected indicator.

Do not display locked weapons as selectable.

3.2 DYNAMIC WEAPON LIST

The selector must automatically adapt to the number of available weapons.

For example:

- 2 weapons: display a compact selection panel.
- 4 weapons: arrange them in a balanced grid.
- 6 weapons: use a responsive grid or scrollable panel.
- 10 or more weapons: use a scrollable collection with optional categories if necessary.

The interface must not become wider or taller uncontrollably.

Do not hardcode a fixed number of weapon buttons.

Generate the selector from the existing weapon data.

When a new weapon is added to the weapon configuration or database, it should automatically appear in the selection interface when unlocked.

Avoid duplicating weapon definitions inside UI code.

3.3 WEAPON SELECTION INTERACTION

When a weapon is selected:

- Update the active weapon immediately.
- Close the selection panel.
- Update the selected weapon icon.
- Display a subtle confirmation animation.
- Preserve the actual weapon system behavior.
- Ensure the selected weapon is used by automatic shooting.

Prevent accidental weapon switching during ordinary movement gestures.

The selector must work correctly with touch and mouse input.

3.4 MOBILE WEAPON SELECTOR

On Android:

- Use compact touch-friendly controls.
- Do not occupy too much screen space.
- Use a small selection panel.
- Support vertical scrolling when the weapon collection is long.
- Keep the selection panel within the visible viewport.
- Prevent the panel from being clipped by screen edges.
- Avoid accidental player movement when interacting with the selector.

The weapon selector must remain flexible when the game receives more weapons in future updates.

