6. ADVANCED POWER-UP NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

This is a major visual improvement.

Currently, when the player collects a power-up, the game mainly displays a text notification in the upper-left corner.

I want this system to be completely redesigned.

Create a professional visual notification system that makes collecting power-ups feel satisfying, rewarding, and immediately understandable.

The new system should use:

- Circular power-up icons.
- Animated appearance.
- Circular countdown indicators.
- Unique pickup effects.
- Clear duration information.
- Subtle visual feedback.

The player must be able to understand which power-up was collected and how much time remains.

6.1 POWER-UP ACTIVE ICON DISPLAY

When the player collects a temporary power-up, display a circular icon in a dedicated HUD area.

Each active power-up should have:

- Circular icon container.
- Unique icon or artwork.
- Power-up identity.
- Animated circular countdown indicator.
- Remaining duration where appropriate.
- Clear active state.

The countdown should use a circular progress outline around the icon.

As the power-up duration decreases:

- The progress outline gradually changes.
- The circular indicator visually tracks the remaining duration.
- The indicator reaches completion when the effect expires.

The countdown must be synchronized with the actual power-up duration.

Do not use a separate visual timer that can become inconsistent with gameplay.

6.2 MULTIPLE ACTIVE POWER-UPS

Support multiple simultaneous power-ups.

When the player collects multiple temporary effects:

- Display their icons in an organized arrangement.
- Use consistent spacing.
- Keep every icon readable.
- Avoid overlapping.
- Avoid covering important HUD elements.
- Support mobile screen widths.

If several power-ups are active, automatically arrange them in a compact horizontal row or responsive layout.

When space is insufficient, adapt the layout without hiding important gameplay information.

Do not create a new fixed button for every possible power-up.

Generate the active power-up display dynamically from the actual active-effect data.

6.3 POWER-UP EXPIRATION

When a temporary power-up expires:

- Its circular progress indicator reaches completion.
- Display a subtle expiration animation.
- Remove the icon smoothly.
- Remove the effect according to the existing gameplay system.

Ensure the visual timer and actual gameplay effect always remain synchronized.

6.4 INSTANTANEOUS POWER-UPS

Not all power-ups have durations.

For instantaneous effects such as immediate health restoration:

- Display a temporary pickup notification.
- Show the appropriate icon.
- Display the actual amount gained.
- Use a short visual animation.
- Remove the notification after a suitable duration.

Do not show a fake countdown for an effect that has no duration.

